\f0\fs40 \cf2 Eye ointment is thicker than eye drops, so it can stay on the eye longer. It is often used at bedtime or whenever longer-lasting lubrication or medication is needed. Because it is thick, it will usually blur vision for a while after it is placed in the eye.\
\
Wash and dry your hands first. If you wear contact lenses, remove them unless your doctor has told you otherwise. Tilt your head back slightly and look up. With one finger, gently pull the lower eyelid down to create a small pocket. Hold the tube close to the eye, but do not let the tip touch the eye, eyelid, lashes, or fingers. Squeeze a small ribbon of ointment into the pocket of the lower lid. A strip about one half centimetre to one centimetre is usually enough unless you were told otherwise.\
\
Let go of the lid and close the eye gently for about 30 to 60 seconds. Do not squeeze tightly. Blink a few times after that to help spread the ointment. Wipe away any excess with a clean tissue.\
\
Important tips:\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li680\fi-360\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 1. If you use both drops and ointment, use the drops first and the ointment last.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li740\fi-420\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 2. Do not share eye ointment with anyone else.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li760\fi-440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 3. Keep the tube tip clean.\
4. Expect temporary blurred vision after use.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
